DockerEngine:

When we install docker on host it install 3 component
dockerd - It used to store all the docker objects ie image, container, volume, network etc
restapi - Its a program send the command that we run on docker cli
docker cli  - it used to run a command

If we want to run docker run command from laptop to other machine where docker is installed need to use below command
docker -H=ip:2378 --tls-verify run nginx

When we run command this is the process actually it will follow
docker cli - run command
rest api  - Take command
dockerd - Manages all docker objects, the it pass to cibatiner d
containerd - It just pull image, manage lifercycle of container and supervise it,then it pass to run c
runc - Its take image and confif and connect with kernel and setup namespace and cgroup to run the container.
In kubernites the dockerd step will not be there it will be directly containerd thats why kubernites wont use docker.

Namespace:
When we boot the system it will create a parent process id ie 1 and under that all other process of the system boot up ie 2, 3 etc we dont have duplicate process id. but for container it has own mount, process, volume etc. So container will create namespace if we run nginx it will start with pid 1 but correspondence nginx will have pid of 300 ie random id based on host that will link to conatiner 1 , that what namespace will do , each containwer can have process id start with 1

cgroup:
To allocate the resource we can use cgroup.
docker run --cpu=0.5 ubuntu - Here we mention 50% of cpu for container when we boot the container
docker run --memory=100m ubuntu - Here we mention 100m for container when we boot the container
If we dont mention container will use all 100%

